  body: "# Order of adjustment for overlapping benefits\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured chapter describes
    an order for considering payment adjustments after checking that benefits are not incompatible, including qualifications
    for hospital deductions and special benefit rules.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe order is a review subject,
    not implemented arithmetic. The full conditions, amounts, historical rules, exceptions and benefit-specific
    provisions remain unmodelled. DMG 17040 cross-refers to ADM M5 for new-style ESA/JSA terminology.\n\n## Inspected
    source passages\n\n- [DMG 17170, PDF page 22](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/62d7b8d5d3bf7f2865c6fe43/dmgch17.pdf#page=22)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 17: Overlapping benefits.\n- [DMG 17180, PDF page 23](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/62d7b8d5d3bf7f2865c6fe43/dmgch17.pdf#page=23)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 17: Overlapping benefits.\n- [DMG 17040, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/62d7b8d5d3bf7f2865c6fe43/dmgch17.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 17: Overlapping benefits.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of
    the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance,
    not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file
    positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve
    extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability
    remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch17` PDF SHA-256: `ce6967960168b301ae0b454df6824017202f6d3f6a14282a7ef0d4778bdac19a`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `c00f0acadb11047d22fe6c046a756a164cc7be254aaebfb91470f2f38201af99`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-incompatible-benefits
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly requires checking incompatibility before considering the stated
      adjustment order.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch17/0022
      quote: "17170 Before considering adjustment of benefits in the order set out below the DM should check that\n\
        the benefits in question are not incompatible (see DMG 17005). If they are not incompatible the order of\n\
        adjustment is as follows\n\n\n1. make adjustments due for other reasons, for example, earnings and Invalidity
        Addition/AP\nadjustments. This is because the overlapping benefits provisions take account of amounts payable.
        An\nexception to this is with hospital in-patients where an adjustment for overlapping benefits should be\n\
        \ncarried out before any hospital in-patient deduction1\n\n\n2. deduct personal Industrial Injuries and
        non-Act benefits from personal Act benefit 2\n\n\n3. deduct personal Act benefit from other personal Act
        benefit 3\n\n\n4. deduct Act and non-Act dependency benefit from other Act dependency benefit 4\n\n\n5.
        deduct Act and non-Act personal benefit payable to dependants in their own right from Act\n\ndependency
        benefit payable for them5\n\n\n6. make any hospital in-patient adjustments6 (see DMG 17161 for exception).\n\
        \n\n                 1 SS (HIP) Regs, reg 18; 2 SS (OB) Regs, reg 6(1); 3 reg 4; 4 reg 7, reg 9; 5 reg 10;
        6 reg 18"
      locator: DMG 17170
  - target: term/dmg-overlapping-benefits
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The ordered steps refer to overlapping-benefit amounts payable and include a hospital-deduction
      exception.
